  "raw": " replaced as second Earl of Stafford, in Liverpool's interest by James Gore-Barlow. He continued to retain his share in several estates and was given an inactive mortgage on Crowborough Castle almost exactly 9 years after HIS death; he died in Poole nine years later of affections caused \"by over indulgence \".\n\nThe Burkes married Prince Henry Lennox, Princesse des Anciens Dukes d’Angoulême (her first husband) in 1834 and the prince royal divorced her a year later and remarried in Dundee. The couple had one son: Angus William, Viscount Keith (1835–1912). His father had been created Earl of Stafford following his success during at least Hunter’s Rebellion and the Battle of Waterloo. At the time of Stafford’s wedding in Dundee, Mackintosh made it clear that Andrew was conducting proceedings against Princess Caroline because she had offended him in a letter; in fact Lord Dig",
